From: Marco Müller <hello@annoyedmilk.ch>
Subject: [PATCH] host: keep the firmware when the ESP32-S31 RCP stream closes

When userspace closes /dev/esp_rcp0, the driver asks for a firmware
restart, so that the next session gets a fresh OpenThread backend.  On
the ESP32-S31 with Linux on the same chip, the firmware cannot restart
without Linux, and the request only replays the boot event.  OpenThread
is not reset, but the driver sets up Wi-Fi again, and the network is
lost.

Keep the firmware incarnation on the ESP32-S31.  A Thread host resets
the RCP with Spinel RESET when it opens the stream.

Upstream: not sent
---
diff --git a/host/esp_rcp.c b/host/esp_rcp.c
--- a/host/esp_rcp.c
+++ b/host/esp_rcp.c
@@ -321,8 +321,14 @@
 	 * worker-owned stateful traffic is flushed/waited first, then the old
 	 * firmware incarnation is destroyed. A subsequent open is rejected while
 	 * recovery is pending by esp_rcp_session_ready().
+	 *
+	 * On the ESP32-S31 with Linux on the same chip, the firmware cannot
+	 * restart without Linux.  A restart request only replays the boot event:
+	 * it does not reset OpenThread, but it stops Wi-Fi.  A Thread host resets
+	 * the RCP with Spinel RESET when it opens the stream, so keep the
+	 * incarnation.
 	 */
-	if (session_current && adapter &&
+	if (!IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_ESP32S31_HOSTED) && session_current && adapter &&
 	    !test_bit(ESP_DRIVER_UNLOADING, &adapter->state_flags) &&
 	    !test_bit(ESP_TRANSPORT_REMOVING, &adapter->state_flags)) {
 		esp_info("RCP userspace session closed; reincarnating firmware to fence backend state\n");
